59,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A, Paid Allocation, seems to address the financial and usage issues directly.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,I support Option A. It creates a revenue stream and prioritizes those who use the spaces.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"I have concerns about Option A, but I see the logic. Option B might be too chaotic.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option A is the most rational choice. It prevents the social friction I was worried about.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,"I am still worried about the workload, but Option A seems the most structured.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@George, what are your specific concerns with Option A?","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, the treasurer's time is a concern, but the income could help offset that.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,I worry about households who cannot afford the charge. But the ward park is also expensive.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, we can set a reasonable rate. The neighbouring block's issue was arrears, not the rate itself.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, that is a good point. The income could fund the maintenance and reduce the treasurer's burden.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"Option C, the lottery, seems arbitrary. It does not account for daily usage.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,Agreed. Option C is too random. Option A is more equitable for those who rely on the spaces.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"Option B, shared racks, might work if we have enough space, but we do not.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,Option B is too risky. It could lead to more conflicts over space.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,I agree. Option A is the best balance of fairness and practicality.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I will vote for Option A.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will vote for Option A.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,"I will vote for Option A, with the caveat that we monitor the impact.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I will vote for Option A.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I will vote for Option A, but we need to plan for the administrative workload.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
